;; Exemptions for `bb check:doc-counts`.
;;
;; Every entry MUST carry a `:why`. The gate rejects one without it rather than
;; honouring it: an allowlist entry with no stated reason is indistinguishable
;; from an unfixed bug, which is the failure mode BOU-250 catalogued.
;;
;; Before adding an entry, check the alternatives — they are usually right:
;;
;;   * A historical document (changelog, ADR, delivered talk, dated design doc)
;;     should be in `excluded-paths` in check_doc_counts.clj, not here. Those
;;     record what was true when written.
;;   * A number that is not a count of libraries — `HTTP 200 for each library`,
;;     `6 of 9 libraries done` — should be handled by `gap-disqualifiers`, so
;;     the same shape never needs allowlisting twice.
;;
;; This file is for the remaining case: live prose that deliberately quotes a
;; number known to be wrong.
;;
;; `:line` is optional; omit it to exempt the whole file.

{:allow
 [{:path "dev-docs/reference/publishing.adoc"
   :line 51
   :why  "Quotes the old wrong count on purpose. The note explains that a previous
          version of this table listed 22 libraries and gave platform two
          dependencies instead of six, so a reader who remembers the old table
          knows it was replaced rather than that they misread it."}

  {:path "dev-docs/reference/publishing.adoc"
   :line 111
   :why  "Quotes the old wrong count on purpose. The comment above the bump command
          records that the previous version hardcoded 22 library names and would
          have left 7 artifacts on the old version silently — the reason the
          command now globs libs/*/build.clj instead of listing names."}]}
